WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.910
Atresia of the duodenum
is a birth defect

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.950
in which the first part of
a baby's small intestine,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.100
called the duodenum, is blocked.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.400
Located between the stomach
and large intestine,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.530
the small intestine absorbs
nutrients from food.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:33.400
The small intestine has
three parts, the duodenum,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:39.100
the jejunum, and the ileum.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:45.310
The duodenum forms during
the sixth week of pregnancy.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.440
Here you can see
the tube that will

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.320
become the digestive system.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.970
The duodenum grows just
below the developing stomach.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.380
The cells inside the
duodenum grow so fast

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.050
that the tube becomes
blocked for a while.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.490
Later, as part of
normal development,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.030
the cells blocking the
inside of the duodenum

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:13.580
die off until the developing
intestine is open again.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.330
By about the 10th week of
pregnancy, for unknown reasons,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.250
the outside wall of the duodenum
may not have grown properly.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.930
In addition, the cells blocking
the inside of the duodenum

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:29.290
may not have died off.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:33.640
As a result, a defect
called duodenal atresia

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:39.540
in which a part of the duodenum
is blocked in one or more ways.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:46.570
It may be blocked by a web
of tissue lining the inside

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:52.800
or a section of the duodenum
may be completely missing.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:59.000
Finally, the duodenum
may be narrowed.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.460
Any of these types of
atresia prevent the baby

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.750
from absorbing
nutrients from milk

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.070
because the fluid can't
pass through the duodenum.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.500
Duodenal atresia is not
immediately life-threatening.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.450
But it will require in
operation within a few days

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.890
after birth to repair
the blocked duodenum.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.410
Before the operation,
a suction tube,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.630
or NG, inserted soon after
birth through the nose or mouth,

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.210
will remove excess fluid
and air from the stomach.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.720
The baby will be given
general anesthesia

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.380
to put him or her to sleep
for the entire operation.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.240
A breathing tube
will be inserted

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.120
through the nose or mouth
and into the windpipe

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.200
to help the baby breathe
during the operation.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.280
Commonly, the surgeon
will make an incision

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.500
under the ribs on
the right side.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.740
Next, the surgeon
will carefully find

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.520
the atresia, or narrow
and blocked part

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.700
of the baby's duodenum.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.390
Two incisions will be
made in the duodenum

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:11.500
above and below the atresia.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:20.880
The surgeon will use sutures to
connect the two openings, thus,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.900
bypassing the atresia.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.940
Finally, the surgeon will
close the skin incision

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:33.900
with dissolvable sutures
or skin closure strips.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.210
After the operation,
the baby will

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.100
be taken to the Neonatal
Intensive Care Unit

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.270
for monitoring.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.330
Pain medication will be given.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:49.250
The baby may continue to receive
antibiotics through the IV.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.600
The baby will be released from
the hospital within two to four

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.040
weeks when the digestive
system is working normally.

